# Ignore data race of freelist
race:freelist_new

# The free side of the same lock-free freelist: ink_freelist_free reads the
# approximate `used` accounting counter (an ink_assert) while another thread
# atomically decrements it. Benign, same class as freelist_new. Surfaces more
# with the io_uring NetVConnection because it frees to a global ClassAllocator
# (hit by every ET_NET thread) rather than a per-thread ProxyAllocator.
race:ink_freelist_free

# InkAtomicList (ATS's lock-free Treiber stack): pop/push intentionally read and write the
# intrusive next-link of the head node without per-field locking -- correctness comes from the
# 128-bit CAS + version counter (ABA), which TSan cannot reason about. Same benign class as the
# freelist entries above (ink_freelist is itself built on this primitive). NOTE: these are
# function-level suppressions, so they cover EVERY InkAtomicList user in the process (event
# queues, freelists, the io_uring fixed-buffer arena's per-class descriptor pools, ...), not any
# one data structure.
race:ink_atomiclist_pop
race:ink_atomiclist_push
